      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before settlers arrived in 1835, the Kickapoo tribe inhabited the land until treaties in 1819 and 1833 opened the prairie to white settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/seymour_illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Seymour sits about 700 feet above sea level in the Sangamon River valley, surrounded by the rolling Grand Prairie and former wetlands now farmed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
